  "conventions": [
    "U1 uses z(phi)=exp(+i phi), matching the first lesson. SU2 and SU3 keep U(theta)=exp(-i theta T), T=Pauli/2 or Gell-Mann/2.",
    "The spinor and vector matrices represent the same SU2 element on distinct spaces; representation dimension is distinct from group dimension.",
    "The balanced interferometer retains the ordered path-spin basis (a up,a down,b up,b down), phase on branch b, and unnormalized port spin amplitudes.",
    "P-1 orbit calculations distinguish the finite action modulo lattice translations from the actual site-fixing space operation.",
    "The colour comparison follows Theta=-i sigma_y K and distinguishes a linear permutation from an antiunitary operation."
  ],
  "verification": [
    "The ten dedicated exercises retain originating lesson IDs and genuinely registered laboratory presets where appropriate.",
    "Production exercise expressions are checked using exact Fraction arithmetic; new laboratory results are checked against independent analytic formulas and public dispatcher fixtures.",
    "English calculation-display audits include the real introductory results and preserve all numerical fields.",
    "Previous 32 Lie and 20 crystal exercises are retained; the remaining unmatched lessons open an unselected bank."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Finite samples illustrate group-theory results; they do not prove every general theorem.",
    "The unit-circle member checks use disclosed numerical tolerances; the exact algebraic condition is stated separately.",
    "These are idealized teaching models, not empirical material predictions or student learning-outcome measurements.",
    "Four advanced Lie lessons and the magnetic-setting lesson still lack dedicated derivations."
  ],
